Z||000006||Neal||11-23-2001||03:18 PM||||Heated mirrors are a GODSEND on cold frosty mornings, one of the first things i looked into when i got my fiero, but two years later, no dice.<P>So another "how did you do it?"||||reg||1
Z||000007||cadaver||11-23-2001||09:34 PM||||I didnt find anything OEM that would fit. I wish it would have been alot easier.<BR>I found a manufacturer that supplies some of the car makers with parts. <BR>So I just adapted the hot plates to fit. Once installed you cant tell the difference, well except on those cold mornings when I can now see whats next to me.<BR>Hey V6GT you have never gone out in the morning and had the mirrors covered in frost? Or do you just not get up early enough? Not being mean. I leave at 5:15 most mornings and they help a whole lot.<BR>I am thinking of putting together some kits for do it yourself installation. What would be a far price?||||reg||1
Z||000008||dragolic@msn.com||11-23-2001||10:48 PM||||Did you look at corvette mirrors.  I had an 86 and the drivers side mirror was heated.  I would think it would be easier to adapt those mirrors.  The vette was a fair weather driving car so I never really saw a use for the heated mirros.  Would come in handy on cold Ohio mornings though.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||cadaver||11-23-2001||11:36 PM||||I usually dont try to find parts that are expensive. More expensive than to bother with the conversion.<BR>How much do complete vette mirrors go for? But if you would like to please do and let me know how it works out.||||reg||1
Z||000010||dragolic@msn.com||11-24-2001||09:12 PM||||I never had to replace the mirrors on my vette.  But I would think that a junkyard would sell them relatively cheap.  It was just a thought.||||reg||1
Z||000011||theogre||11-25-2001||03:01 PM||||I thought JC whitless had mirror heaters. maybe it was just for trucks...<P>I'm not sure what you used. most of the meaters I've had to deal with went between the glass and the mount plate. Hardest part for me was removing the broken glass w/o damaging the heater.<P>The "easiest" way to install a heater that goes between the glass and mount would be to get new glass. Then you can break the old glass if needed to get it off the mount easier. I'm pretty sure the glass for both sides is available thru the MotorMite Help! series.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
